{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Plugin Architecture"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"],"title":"Explanation"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin"},{"text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},{"type":"text","text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management."}]},{"anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call to ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The generic ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write ","type":"text"},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by hand — ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A fifth method, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}]},{"anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app."}]},{"anchor":"Core-Middleware","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Core Middleware"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":" are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"action-agnostic infrastructure"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". They never inspect the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" needs keypaths to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" properties.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" needs "},{"code":"State: Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so it can snapshot and compare."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Domain Plugins","level":3,"anchor":"Domain-Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"domain-specific modules","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" that ship as separate library targets (","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites","text":"Importing at call sites"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"separate library target","type":"text"}]},{"text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_exported import Swidux"},{"text":", but that re-exports ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"core Swidux only"}]},{"type":"text","text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice (","type":"text"},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.*"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.killswitch.*"},{"type":"text","text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallAction"},{"type":"text","text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"that"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" file:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches "},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"code":"import SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches "},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":".ui(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The easy case to forget is a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"View"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" that reads the slice for display — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The fix is to add ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Swidux<Plugin>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to that file."}]},{"anchor":"Comparison","text":"Comparison","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core Middleware"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain Plugins"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action knowledge"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Lifecycle hooks","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns effects","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"State coupling","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" constraint","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wiring"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Construction only","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" library","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Separate library target","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}]}]]]},{"level":2,"text":"The Decision Rule","type":"heading","anchor":"The-Decision-Rule"},{"style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s core middleware — put it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":". If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"yes"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"aside"},{"level":2,"text":"Hook Selection Guide","type":"heading","anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"willReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":" — Capture state ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Handle domain-specific actions "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce(state:action:)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Observe state "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}]},{"type":"text","text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"flush() async","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"text":"Registration Order","anchor":"Registration-Order","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true},{"text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","type":"heading","anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"service-result action","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"KillswitchPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"verdictReceived","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshSucceeded","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — fires on ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"every","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config).","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Do "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state slice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — or a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"derived from it — instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.send","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"snapshot, then writes back via ","type":"text"},{"code":"State.apply","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For a leaf slice that write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a plain assignment whose ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" setter equality-gates ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value-diffing consumer such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", not of any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observers without any extra reducer logic."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Next Steps","anchor":"Next-Steps","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware"}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","title":"Design Principles","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","role":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"title":"Building a Domain Plugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Store","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observation layer.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","title":"PersistencePlugin","abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EntityStore","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","title":"PluginHost","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Undo \/ Redo","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","abstract":[{"text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","title":"Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","role":"collection","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","title":"SwiduxPlugin","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Persistence Middleware","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide"}}}